   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "How often",
   "texto": [
    "**まいにち** (every day), **いつも** (always), **よく** (often), **ときどき** (sometimes). They're going in front of the verb.",
    "**あまり** (not much) and **ぜんぜん** (nothing, never) demand the verb in **negativo**: **あまり しません** (I don't do much), **ぜんぜん みません** (I never see it)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Where and with whom",
   "texto": [
    "**で** marks the place where **se hace** an action: **うち で ほん を よみます** (I read a book at home). Don't confuse him with **に**, which marks where **está** something.",
    "**と** with one person means «with»: **ともだち と** (with a friend).",
    "**します** is «do»: **スポーツ を します** (do sport), **テニス を します** (play tennis)."
   ]
